{
  "about": "Blocks and math spans the server's parser and the browser's must both find in each document (living documents, LD-5 and LD-9). blocks: each block in document order, a parent before its children, as [kind, depth, first line, end line], lines counted from 0 and the end exclusive, without trailing blank lines; a container's lines take in its closing marker. math: each formula as [index of its block, inline or display, its TeX as the parser reads it]. Formulas in an image's description are not spans. The dialect is the workspace's (dollarmath.fixtures.json, mathdelimiters.fixtures.json), with YAML front matter and theorem-like containers (::: lemma) added.",
  "cases": [
    {"name": "front matter, a heading and a paragraph", "markdown": "---\ntitle: Notes\nmacros:\n  \\F: \\mathbb{F}\n---\n# Notes\n\nLet $p$ be prime.\n", "blocks": [["front_matter", 0, 0, 5], ["heading", 0, 5, 6], ["paragraph", 0, 7, 8]], "math": [[2, "inline", "p"]]},
    {"name": "front matter only at the very start", "markdown": "Text.\n\n---\ntitle: no\n---\n", "blocks": [["paragraph", 0, 0, 1], ["thematic_break", 0, 2, 3], ["heading", 0, 3, 5]], "math": []},
    {"name": "front matter that never closes is a thematic break and a paragraph", "markdown": "---\ntitle: open\n", "blocks": [["thematic_break", 0, 0, 1], ["paragraph", 0, 1, 2]], "math": []},
    {"name": "dollar signs that are not math", "markdown": "It costs $5 and $10, or $ x$ and $x $.\n", "blocks": [["paragraph", 0, 0, 1]], "math": []},
    {"name": "escaped dollars", "markdown": "A \\$ sign, \\$x\\$, and $y \\$ z$.\n", "blocks": [["paragraph", 0, 0, 1]], "math": [[0, "inline", "y \\$ z"]]},
    {"name": "double dollars inside a paragraph", "markdown": "So $$x = y$$ holds, and\n$$\nz = w\n$$\nalso.\n", "blocks": [["paragraph", 0, 0, 5]], "math": [[0, "display", "x = y"], [0, "display", "\nz = w\n"]]},
    {"name": "a $$ that never closes", "markdown": "$$\nx = 1\n\nThe rest.\n", "blocks": [["paragraph", 0, 0, 2], ["paragraph", 0, 3, 4]], "math": []},
    {"name": "a labelled equation", "markdown": "$$\na^{p-1} = 1\n$$ (fermat)\n\n$$b = c$$ (my eq)\n", "blocks": [["equation", 0, 0, 3], ["equation", 0, 4, 5]], "math": [[0, "display", "\na^{p-1} = 1\n"], [1, "display", "b = c"]]},
    {"name": "raw HTML stays text", "markdown": "<div class=\"x\">$x$</div>\n\n<script>alert(1)</script>\n", "blocks": [["paragraph", 0, 0, 1], ["paragraph", 0, 2, 3]], "math": [[0, "inline", "x"]]},
    {"name": "headings, setext too", "markdown": "# One $a$\n\nTwo $b$\n---\n\nThree\n=====\n", "blocks": [["heading", 0, 0, 1], ["heading", 0, 2, 4], ["heading", 0, 5, 7]], "math": [[0, "inline", "a"], [1, "inline", "b"]]},
    {"name": "a thematic break", "markdown": "Before.\n\n***\n\nAfter.\n", "blocks": [["paragraph", 0, 0, 1], ["thematic_break", 0, 2, 3], ["paragraph", 0, 4, 5]], "math": []},
    {"name": "lists, nested", "markdown": "- one $a$\n- two\n  - inner $b$\n  - more\n\n1. first\n2. second $c$\n", "blocks": [["list", 0, 0, 4], ["list_item", 1, 0, 1], ["paragraph", 2, 0, 1], ["list_item", 1, 1, 4], ["paragraph", 2, 1, 2], ["list", 2, 2, 4], ["list_item", 3, 2, 3], ["paragraph", 4, 2, 3], ["list_item", 3, 3, 4], ["paragraph", 4, 3, 4], ["list", 0, 5, 7], ["list_item", 1, 5, 6], ["paragraph", 2, 5, 6], ["list_item", 1, 6, 7], ["paragraph", 2, 6, 7]], "math": [[2, "inline", "a"], [7, "inline", "b"], [14, "inline", "c"]]},
    {"name": "a loose list with blank lines", "markdown": "- one\n\n- two\n\n  second paragraph $x$\n", "blocks": [["list", 0, 0, 5], ["list_item", 1, 0, 1], ["paragraph", 2, 0, 1], ["list_item", 1, 2, 5], ["paragraph", 2, 2, 3], ["paragraph", 2, 4, 5]], "math": [[5, "inline", "x"]]},
    {"name": "quotes, with a list and math", "markdown": "> quoted $x$\n> - item $y$\n>\n> more\n", "blocks": [["quote", 0, 0, 4], ["paragraph", 1, 0, 1], ["list", 1, 1, 2], ["list_item", 2, 1, 2], ["paragraph", 3, 1, 2], ["paragraph", 1, 3, 4]], "math": [[1, "inline", "x"], [4, "inline", "y"]]},
    {"name": "a lazy continuation line", "markdown": "> quoted\nlazy $z$\n", "blocks": [["quote", 0, 0, 2], ["paragraph", 1, 0, 2]], "math": [[1, "inline", "z"]]},
    {"name": "a table with math", "markdown": "| $a$ | $a^{16}$ |\n| --- | :---: |\n| 2 | $1$ |\n| \\| | $x \\| y$ |\n", "blocks": [["table", 0, 0, 4]], "math": [[0, "inline", "a"], [0, "inline", "a^{16}"], [0, "inline", "1"], [0, "inline", "x | y"]]},
    {"name": "code, fenced and indented", "markdown": "```python\nx = '$a$'\n```\n\n    $b$ indented\n\nAfter $c$.\n", "blocks": [["code", 0, 0, 3], ["code", 0, 4, 5], ["paragraph", 0, 6, 7]], "math": [[2, "inline", "c"]]},
    {"name": "a fence that never closes", "markdown": "Text $a$.\n\n```\ncode $b$\n\nmore\n", "blocks": [["paragraph", 0, 0, 1], ["code", 0, 2, 6]], "math": [[0, "inline", "a"]]},
    {"name": "a theorem-like container", "markdown": "::: lemma (fermat)\nFor every prime $p$, $a^p \\equiv a$.\n:::\n", "blocks": [["container", 0, 0, 3], ["paragraph", 1, 1, 2]], "math": [[1, "inline", "p"], [1, "inline", "a^p \\equiv a"]]},
    {"name": "nested containers", "markdown": ":::: theorem\nStatement $s$.\n\n::: proof\nBecause $q$.\n:::\n::::\n", "blocks": [["container", 0, 0, 7], ["paragraph", 1, 1, 2], ["container", 1, 3, 6], ["paragraph", 2, 4, 5]], "math": [[1, "inline", "s"], [3, "inline", "q"]]},
    {"name": "same-length markers do not nest", "markdown": "::: lemma\nOuter.\n::: proof\nInner.\n:::\n:::\n", "blocks": [["container", 0, 0, 5], ["paragraph", 1, 1, 2], ["container", 1, 2, 4], ["paragraph", 2, 3, 4], ["paragraph", 0, 5, 6]], "math": []},
